# Normalise line endings to LF in the working tree on EVERY platform.
#
# Without this, Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks the tree out with CRLF, and
# biome's formatter — which emits LF — then reports every single file as misformatted. That is
# exactly how the Windows CI leg failed on PR #2: 37 errors, one per file, each a whole-file diff
# whose only difference was an invisible carriage return.
#
# This is the fix rather than relaxing the formatter, because the formatter was right: the repo's
# committed content is LF and should stay LF wherever it is checked out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish files that must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
